# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_delivery_key_disambiguation.py" "DELIVERY-KEY DISAMBIGUATION GATE: PASS" "delivery_key headerless disambiguation" "delivery_key headerless disambiguation (small-findings root fix, durability): on the no-X-GitHub-Delivery path (local/smee/dev or a header-stripped request) the durable-inbox key is a content hash that USED to hash the SANITIZED payload — but sanitize_payload drops the distinguishing fields (commit messages, PR bodies, titles, the delivery id), so two SEMANTICALLY-DIFFERENT deliveries could sanitize to byte-identical content -> the same 'local-…' key -> the enqueue's ON CONFLICT MERGED two distinct events onto ONE row = a silently-LOST delivery. ROOT fix: delivery_key now hashes the RAW (pre-sanitization) payload on the fallback (it retains the dropped fields) — two raw-distinct headerless deliveries get DISTINCT keys (two DB rows, no merge), a TRUE redelivery (identical raw payload) keeps the SAME key (one row, idempotent), and a header-bearing delivery still keys by X-GitHub-Delivery (a 503-redeliver is one row). Proven through a real DeliveryStore.submit + the enqueue ON CONFLICT against a live DB" "delivery_key headerless disambiguation (two distinct headerless deliveries no longer merge onto one durable row — raw-payload hash separates them while a true redelivery stays idempotent) — webhook durability" 16
